To process multiple independent orders in a single request where each order is committed atomically (all-or-none per order) without a failure in one order affecting the others, use the **Composite Graph API** (`/services/data/vXX.0/composite/graph`).

Each graph in the `graphs` array acts as an isolated transactional unit of work identified by its `graphId` (`SO-1001` and `SO-1002`). Within each graph:
1. A `PATCH` subrequest upserts the `Account` using the `Customer_Number__c` external ID in the URL path.
2. A `POST` subrequest creates the `Opportunity` and links it to the upserted account via `@{referenceId.id}`.

```http
POST /services/data/v60.0/composite/graph HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "graphs": [
    {
      "graphId": "SO-1001",
      "compositeRequest": [
        {
          "method": "PATCH",
          "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Account/Customer_Number__c/C-1001",
          "referenceId": "acct_1001",
          "body": {
            "Name": "Alder Creek Cafe"
          }
        },
        {
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Opportunity",
          "referenceId": "opp_1001",
          "body": {
            "Name": "Web order SO-1001",
            "StageName": "Closed Won",
            "CloseDate": "2026-09-26",
            "Amount": 1250,
            "AccountId": "@{acct_1001.id}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "graphId": "SO-1002",
      "compositeRequest": [
        {
          "method": "PATCH",
          "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Account/Customer_Number__c/C-2002",
          "referenceId": "acct_1002",
          "body": {
            "Name": "Birch Lane Bakery"
          }
        },
        {
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Opportunity",
          "referenceId": "opp_1002",
          "body": {
            "Name": "Web order SO-1002",
            "StageName": "Closed Won",
            "CloseDate": "2026-09-26",
            "Amount": 980,
            "AccountId": "@{acct_1002.id}"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

To create all three records in a single transactional REST API call while guaranteeing that the `Asset` is inserted before the `Service_Request__c` trigger runs:

1. **Use the Composite API (`/services/data/v60.0/composite`)** with `"allOrNone": true` so the entire transaction rolls back if any subrequest fails.
2. **Set `"collateSubrequests": false`**. By default (`true`), the Composite API analyzes `@{referenceId}` dependencies and collates independent subrequests into batches. Because `newRequest` has no `@{...}` reference to `newAsset` or `newAccount`, default collation would execute `newRequest` in the first batch alongside `newAccount`—before `newAsset` is created—causing the `Service_Request__c` before-insert trigger to fail. Disabling collation enforces strict sequential execution in the order the subrequests are listed.

```http
POST /services/data/v60.0/composite HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "allOrNone": true,
  "collateSubrequests": false,
  "compositeRequest": [
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Account",
      "referenceId": "newAccount",
      "body": {
        "Name": "Hollis Outdoor Supply"
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Asset",
      "referenceId": "newAsset",
      "body": {
        "Name": "Trailhead Kiosk 3000",
        "SerialNumber": "SN-88213",
        "AccountId": "@{newAccount.id}"
      }
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Service_Request__c",
      "referenceId": "newRequest",
      "body": {
        "Subject__c": "Installation",
        "Serial_Number__c": "SN-88213"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

To create or update the `Account` without knowing whether it already exists in Salesforce, use a `PATCH` request against the sObject External ID endpoint (`/sobjects/Account/ERP_Customer_Id__c/ERP-10042`). To link the parent account without querying its Salesforce `Id`, reference the `Parent` relationship object in the JSON payload using its `ERP_Customer_Id__c` External ID.

